  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Weather sphere, caster level 5th.</p>\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> When you are using control weather to create Wind of severity level 4 or above in an area of Aridity severity level 3 or above, you may cause a dust storm even if there is no sand or dust in the area. Dust storms blow fine grains of sand that obscure vision, smother unprotected flames, and can even choke protected flames (50% chance). At Wind severity level 5, a dust storm deals 1d3 points of nonlethal damage each round to anyone caught out in the open without shelter and also poses a choking hazard (see Drowning, except that a character with a scarf or similar protection across her mouth and nose does not begin to choke until after a number of rounds equal to 10 + her Constitution score).</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/weather#toc103\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
